e Walk, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "257670"} "High Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9030952"} "Long Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9030966"} "Triple Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "257754"} "Shot Put, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "257771"} "Discus Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "257788"} "Hammer Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "257805"} "Javelin Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "257822"} "Heptathlon, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "65838"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "66549"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "302198"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "359130"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000790"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2013959"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/112"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Pole Vault, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "16 – 18 August 2008"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/813"} "Beijing Guojia Tiyuchang, Beijing Aolinpike Gongyuan, Beijing"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/257692"} "36 from 24 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/88456"} "Yelena Isinbayeva"] " was an overwhelming favorite in the women’s pole vault and she did not disappoint. The Russian defending champion and 2005 and 2007 World Champion had also set the last 11 world records, starting in 2004, with her last two coming earlier in 2008. American " [:a {:href "/athletes/114797"} "Jenn Stuczynski"] " was the second choice but Isinbayeva would likely have to no height for her to win. Stuczynski did not think so, stating after the Olympics Trials, “I hope we do some damage and, you know, kick some Russian butt.” Isi heard the comment and it only served to rev her up. Isinbayeva opened with a first-vault clearance at 4.70 (15-5). Stuczynski led after clearing 4.80 (15-9), and was the only other vaulter left, as Isinbayeva passed to 4.85 (15-11). The two then played a game of cat-and-mouse passing, as Stuczynski passed that height. She jumped at 4.90 (16-0¾), at which the Russian passed, but went out after three misses. Isinbayeva now had the gold medal but she was not done. She cleared 4.95 (16-2¾) on her third try and then had the bar moved to the world record height of 5.05 (16-6¾). She needed three attempts but got over the bar for her 12th outdoor world record."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2784"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/88456"} "Yelena Isinbayeva"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RUS.png"}] "RUS"]] [:td {} "4.60 (1)"] [:td {} "5.05 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "3276"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/114797"} "Jenn Stuczynski"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "4.50 (=2)"] [:td {} "4.80 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2778"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/88449"} "Svetlana Feofa